From 7af609549bce52086a1c501409b77203869eedc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shardul Bankar <shardul.b@mpiricsoftware.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:55:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] mptcp: open the delegated-action kcov section per subflow
 in mptcp_napi_poll

The deferred send push reached through the NAPI-delegated path was
bracketed inside mptcp_subflow_process_delegated(), around the
MPTCP_DELEGATE_SEND branch only. The rest of the delegated processing
(the sndbuf sync, the third-ACK scheduling) and mptcp_napi_poll() itself,
which runs in the NET_RX softirq on the delegated-action device, stayed
outside any section: a coverage-guided fuzzer sees none of
mptcp_napi_poll()'s PCs although every join and every deferred push goes
through it.

Move the section to the poll loop, one per dequeued subflow and keyed on
that subflow's msk. The per-CPU delegated list mixes subflows of
different msks, so a single section at poll entry would attribute all of
them to the first msk's creator; and kcov forbids nesting a softirq
section in another, so the loop-level section and the former inner one
cannot coexist. The msk is read once, under the subflow lock, so that
start and stop use the same key.

The other caller of mptcp_subflow_process_delegated(),
tcp_release_cb_override(), runs in process context from release_sock(),
where the softirq-guarded helper was already a no-op and per-task kcov
records the work; it loses nothing.

Nesting check: the loop body reaches __mptcp_subflow_push_pending(),
__mptcp_sync_sndbuf() and schedule_3rdack_retransmission(); none of them
calls a bracketed site (the option-parser and validator sections are
receive-path only, __mptcp_check_push() is called only from options.c,
and the transmit path hands the segment to netif_rx(), which defers to a
later softirq). A NAPI poll that runs while mptcp_worker()'s
task-context section is open (release_sock() -> local_bh_enable()) is
the softirq-interrupts-task case kcov supports explicitly.

Instrumentation-only, no functional change; no-op under CONFIG_KCOV=n.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PnC9KL4QuZ7vdAomuT6sTC
---
 net/mptcp/protocol.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/protocol.c b/net/mptcp/protocol.c
index a701892ad338..0e96b857cc89 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/protocol.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/protocol.c
@@ -3999,11 +3999,9 @@ void mptcp_subflow_process_delegated(struct sock *ssk, long status)
 
 	if (status & BIT(MPTCP_DELEGATE_SEND)) {
 		mptcp_data_lock(sk);
-		if (!sock_owned_by_user(sk)) {
-			mptcp_kcov_remote_start(mptcp_sk(sk));
+		if (!sock_owned_by_user(sk))
 			__mptcp_subflow_push_pending(sk, ssk, true);
-			mptcp_kcov_remote_stop(mptcp_sk(sk));
-		} else
+		else
 			__set_bit(MPTCP_PUSH_PENDING, &mptcp_sk(sk)->cb_flags);
 		mptcp_data_unlock(sk);
 	}
@@ -4861,8 +4859,19 @@ static int mptcp_napi_poll(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 	delegated = container_of(napi, struct mptcp_delegated_action, napi);
 	while ((subflow = mptcp_subflow_delegated_next(delegated)) != NULL) {
 		struct sock *ssk = mptcp_subflow_tcp_sock(subflow);
+		struct mptcp_sock *msk;
 
 		bh_lock_sock_nested(ssk);
+		/* Attribute this subflow's delegated actions (deferred push,
+		 * sndbuf sync, third-ACK scheduling) to the task that created
+		 * its msk.  One section per subflow: the per-CPU list mixes
+		 * subflows of different msks, and a softirq section must not
+		 * nest in another, so the section lives here rather than in
+		 * mptcp_subflow_process_delegated().  The key is read once so
+		 * that start and stop agree.
+		 */
+		msk = mptcp_sk(subflow->conn);
+		mptcp_kcov_remote_start(msk);
 		if (!sock_owned_by_user(ssk)) {
 			mptcp_subflow_process_delegated(ssk, xchg(&subflow->delegated_status, 0));
 		} else {
@@ -4874,6 +4883,7 @@ static int mptcp_napi_poll(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget)
 			smp_wmb();
 			clear_bit(MPTCP_DELEGATE_SCHEDULED, &subflow->delegated_status);
 		}
+		mptcp_kcov_remote_stop(msk);
 		bh_unlock_sock(ssk);
 		sock_put(ssk);
 
